# Without this file, Git on Windows turns every LF in the object store into a
# CRLF in the working tree. The release workflow runs on windows-latest and so
# received different files than the development machine. Vite tripped over
# exactly that: a line comment directly before an `import` made the import
# analysis produce invalid code with CRLF, and the test run aborted with
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token".
#
# The object store contains LF everywhere anyway; this only keeps the working
# copy the same.
* text=auto eol=lf

# None of these should be touched by Git as text.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.nupkg binary
*.exe binary
